INSERT INTO `ai_question_drafts` VALUES (1,'To create visualizations and charts','To detect incorrect, incomplete, inconsistent, or irrelevant data','To perform statistical analysis on raw data','To design databases and data models',1,'2026-11-09 12:47:14.915049','EASY','Definition. Data Cleaning is the process of detecting incorrect, incomplete, inconsistent, or irrelevant data.',_binary '','Data cleaning is defined as the process of detecting incorrect, incomplete, inconsistent, or irrelevant data. This is explicitly stated in the section text.','What is the primary purpose of data cleaning in the analytics pipeline?',0,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:11.746738',38,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(2,'Missing Values','Duplicate Records','Inconsistent Formatting','Data Encryption',3,'2026-11-09 12:47:14.926049','MEDIUM','Common Data Issues\nMissing Values... Duplicate Records... Inconsistent Formatting...',_binary '\0','The text lists missing values, duplicate records, and inconsistent formatting as common data issues. Data encryption is not mentioned in the context of data quality problems.','Which of the following is NOT a common data quality issue mentioned in the text?',0,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:06.364440',37,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(3,'It can handle large datasets with millions of records','It has built-in tools for cleaning and transformation','It automatically detects all data quality issues without user input','It eliminates the need for manual data verification',1,'2026-11-09 12:47:14.935048','EASY','Why Use Excel for Data Cleaning?\no Widely used in industry and education.\no Built-in tools for cleaning and transformation.',_binary '','The text explicitly states that Excel has built-in tools for cleaning and transformation as a key advantage.','What is a key advantage of using Excel for data cleaning according to the text?',0,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:14.138601',39,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(4,'CLEAN()','TRIM()','PROPER()','SUBSTITUTE()',1,'2026-11-09 12:47:54.375461','EASY','• Removes extra spaces from text.\n• Syntax: =TRIM(text)',_binary '','The TRIM() function removes extra spaces from text, as stated in the section text.','Which Excel function is used to remove extra spaces from text?',1,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:15.006949',40,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(5,'REPLACE()','SUBSTITUTE()','CONCAT()','VALUE()',1,'2026-11-09 12:47:54.385460','EASY','• Replaces specific text within a string.\n• Syntax: =SUBSTITUTE(text_ref, old_text, new_text)',_binary '','The SUBSTITUTE() function replaces specific text within a string, as described in the section text.','Which Excel function is used to replace specific text within a string?',1,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:15.818405',41,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(6,'To handle conditional replacement.','To prevent formula errors.','To combine different cells into one cell.','To convert text dates to date values.',1,'2026-11-09 12:47:54.393459','MEDIUM','• Prevents formula errors.\n• Used when results are error (like #DIV/0!, #N/A, #VALUE!)\n• Syntax: =IFERROR(value, value_if_error)',_binary '','The IFERROR() function prevents formula errors when results are error types like #DIV/0! or #N/A, as explained in the section text.','What is the purpose of the IFERROR() function in Excel?',1,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:16.774501',42,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(7,'AVERAGEIFS()','SUMIF()','AVERAGEIF()','COUNTIF()',2,'2026-11-09 12:48:38.873969','EASY','Purpose: Average or Sum cells based on one condition\nSyntax: \n =AVERAGEIF(range, criteria, [average_range])\n =SUMIF(range, criteria, [sum_range])',_binary '','The AVERAGEIF() function is designed to calculate the average of cells based on a single condition, such as averaging sales for a specific region.','Which Excel function is used to calculate the average of sales data for a specific region?',2,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:19.349738',43,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(8,'To sort data alphabetically','To split text into multiple columns based on delimiters','To calculate summary statistics','To create charts from data',1,'2026-11-09 12:48:38.881969','EASY','Text-to-Columns Feature\nSplits text into multiple columns.\nUsed when you have datasets that have delimiters.',_binary '','The Text-to-Columns feature is used to split text into separate columns when there are delimiters present in the dataset.','What is the primary purpose of the Text-to-Columns feature in Excel?',2,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:20.363042',44,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(9,'Step 1: Calculate the Summary Statistics','Step 2: Apply Sturges\' Formula for Number of Bins','Step 3: Calculate the Bin Width','Step 4: Create the Bin Upper and Lower Limits',1,'2026-11-09 12:48:38.890969','MEDIUM','Step 2: Apply Sturges\' Formula for Number of Bins\nIn a new cell, calculate the ideal number of classes (bins or k):\nFormula: \n =ROUND(1 + 3.322 * LOG10(COUNT(table[data])), 0)',_binary '','Sturges\' Rule is applied in Step 2 to determine the ideal number of bins for a histogram.','Which step involves calculating the ideal number of bins for a histogram using Sturges\' Rule?',2,'APPROVED','2026-11-09 12:50:21.533808',45,1,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(10,'Select Insert Column or Bar Chart and choose Clustered Column.','Highlight cells C2:D8 before inserting the chart.','Right-click any bar on the chart, select Format Data Series, and change the Gap Width to 0%.','Go to the Insert tab in the Excel ribbon.',2,'2026-11-09 12:48:50.177799','EASY','To make it a true histogram with no gaps between bars, right-click any bar on the chart, select Format Data Series, and change the Gap Width to 0%.',_binary '','The text explicitly states that to make a true histogram with no gaps between bars, the user must right-click any bar on the chart, select Format Data Series, and change the Gap Width to 0%.','What is the correct step to create a histogram with no gaps between bars in Excel according to the provided text?',3,'APPROVED','202