 the correct choice.','Which of the following best describes structured data?',0,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:12:26.477428',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(72,'Age','Temperature','Customer Reviews','Income',2,'2026-11-10 09:12:26.485428','MEDIUM','Qualitative Data: o Descriptive and categorical (labels) o Examples: Customer Reviews, Colors, Job Titles',_binary '\0','The text categorizes qualitative data as \'descriptive and categorical (labels)\' with examples including \'customer reviews, colors, job titles,\' which matches the correct choice.','Which of the following is an example of qualitative data?',0,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:12:26.485428',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(73,'They are always generated within an organization.','They are less specific to the current research problem.','They are primarily used for internal sales records.','They require direct collection from primary sources.',1,'2026-11-10 09:12:57.666308','EASY','o Cost-effective and time-efficient, but less specific to the current research problem',_binary '','Secondary data sources are described as being \'cost-effective and time-efficient, but less specific to the current research problem,\' which aligns with choice B.','Which of the following is a characteristic of secondary data sources?',1,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:12:57.666308',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(74,'Market data from public datasets','Social media analytics','Employee metrics','Industry analysis reports',2,'2026-11-10 09:12:57.675308','EASY','o Sales records, employee metrics',_binary '','Internal data includes \'employee metrics\' as it is generated within an organization, according to the text.','Which of the following is an example of internal data?',1,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:12:57.675308',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(75,'Slovin-Yamane Formula','Cochran Formula','None of the above','Both Slovin-Yamane and Cochran Formulas',1,'2026-11-10 09:12:57.683310','MEDIUM','Cochran\'s formula is used to determine the sample size needed to estimate a population proportion when the population is large or its size is initially treated as infinite.',_binary '','The Cochran formula is explicitly stated as being used for estimating population proportions when the population is large or treated as infinite.','Which formula is appropriate when estimating a population proportion with a large or infinite population size?',1,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:12:57.683310',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(76,'Interval Level','Ordinal Level','Ratio Level','Nominal Level',3,'2026-11-10 09:13:30.539831','EASY','Nominal Level\no Categories with no inherent order\no Names, assignments and labels',_binary '','The nominal level of measurement involves categories with no inherent order, such as names, assignments, and labels. This is explicitly stated in the section text under \'Levels of Measurement - Nominal Level\'.','Which level of measurement has categories with no inherent order and is used for names, assignments, and labels?',2,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:13:30.539831',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(77,'Mean','Mode','Median','Pearson Correlation',2,'2026-11-10 09:13:30.547833','MEDIUM','Ordinal: Median, Spearman Correlation',_binary '','The median and Spearman correlation are statistical methods typically associated with the ordinal level of measurement. The section text under \'Common Statistical Methods by Level\' specifies that the median is used for ordinal data.','Which statistical method is commonly used for data at the ordinal level?',2,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:13:30.547833',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(78,'To increase the number of datasets','To identify and correct errors, inconsistencies, and inaccuracies in datasets','To remove all outliers from the dataset','To transform data into a different format',1,'2026-11-10 09:13:30.554831','EASY','Data Cleaning\no The process of identifying and correcting errors, inconsistencies, and inaccuracies in datasets',_binary '','Data cleaning involves identifying and correcting errors, inconsistencies, and inaccuracies in datasets. This is clearly outlined in the section text under \'Data Cleaning\'.','What is a key objective of data cleaning in the data preparation process?',2,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:13:30.554831',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(79,'To increase the computational complexity of models','To make numeric variables comparable by standardizing their scales','To reduce the number of features in a dataset','To eliminate all numerical values from the dataset',1,'2026-11-10 09:13:44.194223','EASY','o Techniques used to standardize numeric variables so they are on a comparable scale',_binary '','Feature scaling is used to standardize numeric variables so they are on a comparable scale, which prevents features with large ranges from dominating models and improves algorithm performance.','What is the primary purpose of feature scaling in data analytics?',3,'PENDING','2026-11-10 09:13:44.194223',NULL,10,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(80,'The study of people and computer technology and the ways these influence each other.','The design of hardware and software for mainframe computers and specialists.','The creation of text-based command line interfaces for expert users.','The optimization of business productivity through automated data processing.',0,'2026-11-12 12:38:42.399423','EASY','Human–Computer Interaction is “the study of people and computer technology and the ways these influence each other.” (Preece, Rogers, & Sharp, 2015)',_binary '','According to Preece, Rogers, & Sharp (2015), HCI is formally defined as \'the study of people and computer technology and the ways these influence each other.\'','What is the formal definition of Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) according to Preece, Rogers, & Sharp (2015)?',0,'PENDING','2026-11-12 12:38:42.399423',NULL,21,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(81,'Command Line Interfaces (CLI) Era (1960s–1980s)','Early Computing Era (1940s–1960s)','WIMP Model / Graphical User Interfaces (1980s–1990s)','Mobile and Touch-Based Computing (mid-2000s–2010s)',1,'2026-11-12 12:38:42.413375','MEDIUM','Early Computing Era (1940s–1960s) o use of mainframe computers that occupied entire rooms o Used by trained specialists only o Interaction via punch cards o Characteristics: Batch processing, no real-time interaction',_binary '','The Early Computing Era (1940s–1960s) was characterized by mainframe computers that occupied entire rooms, used by trained specialists via punch cards with batch processing and no real-time interaction.','During which historical era of HCI did computing feature batch processing, room-sized mainframe computers, and interaction via punch cards by trained specialists?',0,'PENDING','2026-11-12 12:38:42.413375',NULL,21,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(82,'The Human Component','The Computer Component','The Interaction Component','The Context of Use',2,'2026-11-12 12:38:42.421348','EASY','o Refers to the communication between users and systems. o Includes: (IPOF Model) • Input • Process • Output • Feedback o Interaction is two-way and continuous',_binary '','The Interaction Component refers to the communication between users and systems, including the IPOF Model (Input, Process, Output, Feedback), and is described as continuous and two-way.','Which core component of HCI includes the IPOF Model (Input, Process, Output, Feedback) and represents the two-way and continuous communication between users and systems?',0,'PENDING','2026-11-12 12:38:42.421348',NULL,21,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(83,'Logical navigation','Error-tolerant design','Creates confusion or frustration','Seamless performance',2,'2026-11-12 12:38:44.098514','EASY','Creates confusion or frustration',_binary '','The text explicitly states that an ineffective design creates confusion or frustration.','What is one of the consequences of an ineffective design according to the course orientation text?',1,'PENDING','2026-11-12 12:38:44.098514',NULL,21,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(84,'Overloaded screens','Logical navigation','Clear functions','Error-tolerant design',0,'2026-11-12 12:38:44.109477','MEDIUM','Overloaded screens',_binary '','The text lists \'Overloaded screens\' as a characteristic of ineffective design.','Which of the following is listed as a characteristic of ineffective design?',1,'PENDING','2026-11-12 12:38:44.109477',NULL,21,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(85,'The study of people and computer technology and the ways these influence each other.','The process of building hardware components for mainframe computers.','The study of programming languages and database management systems.','The technical engineering of microchips and circuit boards.',0,'2026-11-12 14:37:45.046535','EASY','Human–Computer Interaction is “the study of people and computer technology and the ways these influence each other.” (Preece, Rogers, & Sharp, 2015)',_binary '','Preece, Rogers, & Sharp (2015) formally define HCI as \'the study of people and computer technology and the ways these influence each other.\'','According to the presentation, what is the formal definition of Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)?',0,'PENDING','2026-11-12 14:37:45.046535',NULL,22,NULL,0,'ENUMERATION',NULL),(86,'WIMP Model / Graphical User Interfaces (1980s–1990s)','Command Line Interfaces (CLI) Era (1960s–1980s)','Mobile and Touch-Based Computing (mid-2000s–2010s)','Modern Natural User Interfaces (2010s–present)',1,'2026-11-12 14:37:45.059096','MEDIUM','Command Line Interfaces (CLI) Era (1960s–1980s) o Text-based interaction o Required memorization of commands o Little to no visual feedback o High cognitive load on users',_binary '','The Command Line Interfaces (CLI) Era from the 1960s to the 1980s was characterized by text-based interaction, command memorization, little to no visual feedback, and high cognitive load.','During which era of HCI history did computing feature text-based interaction, require memorization of commands, and involve high cognitive load 